hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1175","[AI-translation] Hudhaifah reported, raised to the Prophet: Do not say, ""What Allah willed and so-and-so willed,"" but say, ""What Allah willed, then so-and-so willed."
"1176","[AI-translation] Sahl bin Hanif reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, narrated to him, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to me: ""You are my messenger to Makkah, so convey to them my greetings of peace, and say to them: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, commands you to do three things: Do not swear by your fathers"" — in a narration: ""by other than Allah"" — ""and when you relieve yourselves, do not face the Qiblah nor turn your backs to it, and do not clean yourselves with a bone or dung."
"1177","[AI-translation] Ibn Buraidah reported from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever swears by trustworthiness is not one of us."
"1178","[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Buraidah reported from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: He is not one of us who swears by trustworthiness, and he is not one of us who incites a man against his wife or his servant."
"1179","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah reported: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: A false oath promotes the sale of merchandise but obliterates the earnings — in a narration: the blessings."
"1180","[AI-translation] Abu Umamah bin Tha'labah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: Whoever usurps the property of a Muslim man by a false oath, it becomes a black spot in his heart, which nothing will change until the Day of Resurrection."
"1181","[AI-translation] Uqbah bin Amir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: A vow is merely an oath; its expiation is the expiation of an oath."
"1182","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""A vow is only that by which the Face of Allah is sought."
"1183","[AI-translation] 'As: The wife of Abu Dharr came riding al-Qaswa, the mount of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, until she stopped it near the mosque and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I vowed that if Allah saved me on it, I would certainly eat from its liver and its hump!"" He said: ""What an evil reward you have given it. This is not a vow; a vow is only that by which the Face of Allah is sought."
"1184","[AI-translation] Dahhak, who said: A man vowed during the time of the Prophet, peace be upon him, to slaughter at Buwanah. He came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: ""I have vowed to slaughter at Buwanah."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Was there any idol of the idols of Jahiliyyah worshipped there?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Was there any festival of their festivals held there?"" He said: ""No."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Fulfill your vow, for there is no fulfilling a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in severing ties of kinship, nor in what the son of Adam does not possess."
"1185","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""A vow is of two types: whatever is for Allah, its expiation is to fulfill it; and whatever is for the Shaytan, there is no fulfilling it, and upon it is the expiation of an oath."
"1186","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ""A vow does not bring upon the son of Adam anything that I have not decreed upon him, but it is something by which I extract from the miser. He gives to Me upon it what he would not give out of miserliness."" And in another narration: ""what he would not have given Me before."
"1187","[AI-translation] Juhani, who said: My sister vowed to walk to the Ka'bah barefoot and bareheaded. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, came upon her and said: ""What is the matter with her?"" They said: ""She vowed to walk to the Ka'bah barefoot and bareheaded!"" He said: ""Command her to ride, wear a khimar, (perform Hajj), and (offer a hadi)."
"1188","On the authority of Ibn Abbas that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""I saw tonight in a dream a canopy dripping with butter and honey, and I see people scooping from it — the one who takes much and the one who takes little. And there was a rope extending from the earth to the heaven, and I saw you take hold of it and ascend. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and it broke, then it was reconnected for him and he ascended."" Abu Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah! By my father and mother, let me interpret it."" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""Interpret it."" He said: ""As for the canopy, it is Islam. As for that which drips from it of honey and butter, it is the Quran, its sweetness dripping. So the one who takes much is the one who takes much of the Quran, and the one who takes little is the one who takes little. As for the rope extending from the heaven to the earth, it is the Truth which you are upon; you take hold of it and Allah raises you, then a man takes hold of it and rises, then another man takes hold of it and rises, then another man takes hold of it and it breaks for him, then it is reconnected for him and he rises."" He said: ""Inform me, O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother! Did I get it right or wrong?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""You got some right and some wrong."" He said: ""By Allah, you must tell me what I got wrong."" He said: ""Do not swear."""
